/*  PHASE A CLASSIFICATION WALK -- all 78 Grokking rules, read-only.
    No emission, no installs, no dispatch movement: dumpRulePlans is
    ruleOrRefuse + planRule + printPlan (genParse.rtn:558-566), all cerr.

    ⚠ A1 -- THE COMPLETENESS GUARD, AND IT IS THE POINT OF THE FILE'S SHAPE.
    CLAIM KANT-40 kills a parse SILENTLY at exit 0: one bad construct and every
    statement after it is dropped with no diagnostic. That is a silent-death
    class inside the very act this file performs 78 times, so a missing plan
    would read as A REFUSAL when it is actually A RUN THAT STOPPED.
    Every rule therefore carries its own completion marker, emitted AFTER its
    dump on the SAME STREAM (cerr, so ordering is by flush and not by luck):
        PLAN <name>      ... from dumpRulePlans
        DONE <name>      ... from here, only if the walk reached this line
    A rule with a PLAN and no DONE is UNKNOWN -- walk incomplete -- and must
    never be scored as a refusal. The foot sentinel says the whole walk ran.  */
